0.5.1b:
- [x] Chat: honor a `?llm_model=` URL param on the chat page — pin the model picker to the requested model (validated against the real dropdown options) and persist it to the session `llmModel` cookie, so funnels that need an image-capable model (e.g. the mothership picture-to-html flow, where the default DeepSeek v4 Flash can't see images) can hand users off to Gemini 3 Flash instead of the image-blind default. Unknown keys are ignored and the param is stripped from the URL after load. Browser-smoke coverage added in Leonardo e2e.

0.5.1c:
- [x] Add the ability to do a Git Pull to receive updates from a different Leo instance (such as pulling changes from a dev instance into a prod instance). Adds a "check for updates" (cloud-arrow-down) button next to the existing push button in the History panel: it shows an "N updates available" badge when the box is behind its remote, a one-click "Update now" that does `git pull --ff-only` and restarts the llamapress container so the new code goes live, and a branch switcher to checkout+pull a different branch. Built for the two-VM workflow (push from a dev box, pull on prod) and kept dead-simple for non-technical operators. A fast-forward blocked by local edits surfaces a plain-language message ("you have file changes on this version that conflict… commit or discard them before pulling this update") instead of raw git output. New endpoints: GET /api/git/remote-status, POST /api/git/pull, POST /api/git/checkout (branch validated against the real remote list). pytest coverage in app/tests/test_git_pull.py.

